###############################################
### SETUP GITHUB WEBHOOK
###############################################

# To set up a real GitHub webhook:
# 
# 1. Go to your GitHub repository
# 2. Settings → Webhooks → Add webhook
# 3. Payload URL: http://your-server:8080/api/webhooks/github
#    (Use ngrok for local testing: https://ngrok.com)
# 4. Content type: application/json
# 5. Secret: Set the same value as GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET env var
# 6. Events: Select "Let me select individual events"
#    - Check "Pull requests"
# 7. Active: Check this box
# 8. Add webhook
#
# For local testing with ngrok:
# 1. Install ngrok: https://ngrok.com/download
# 2. Run: ngrok http 8080
# 3. Copy the HTTPS URL (e.g., https://abc123.ngrok.io)
# 4. Use as Payload URL: https://abc123.ngrok.io/api/webhooks/github

###

###############################################
### WEBHOOK SECRET CONFIGURATION
###############################################

# Set environment variable:
# Windows PowerShell:
# $env:GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET = "your_secret_here"
#
# Linux/Mac:
# export GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_secret_here
#
# The secret is used to validate that webhooks come from GitHub
# Generate a strong random secret:
# - Use: openssl rand -hex 32
# - Or any password generator

###

###############################################
### WEBHOOK EVENTS HANDLED
###############################################

# Action: "opened" - New PR created
#   - Creates new PullRequest entity in database
#   - Sets analysisStatus to "pending"
#
# Action: "synchronize" - New commits pushed to PR
#   - Updates headSha
#   - Resets analysisStatus to "pending"
#
# Action: "closed" - PR closed or merged
#   - Updates state to "closed" or "merged"
#   - Sets closedAt and mergedAt timestamps
#
# Action: "reopened" - Closed PR reopened
#   - Updates state back to "open"

###

###############################################
### TESTING WORKFLOW
###############################################

# STEP 1: Verify endpoint is accessible (Test #1)
# STEP 2: Create a repository in the database first
#   - Use: POST /repositories (manual add)
#   - Or: POST /repositories/sync/github (from GitHub)
#   - Ensure full_name matches "testuser/test-repo" in webhook payload
# STEP 3: Send PR opened event (Test #3)
# STEP 4: Verify PR was created: GET /pull-requests
# STEP 5: Send synchronize event (Test #4)
# STEP 6: Verify PR was updated with new SHA
# STEP 7: Send closed event (Test #5)
# STEP 8: Verify PR state changed to "merged"

###

###############################################
### DATABASE VERIFICATION
###############################################

# After sending webhooks, check MongoDB:
# 
# Webhook Events Collection:
# db.webhook_events.find().sort({createdAt: -1})
#
# Pull Requests Collection:
# db.pull_requests.find({prNumber: 1})
#
# Check status field in webhook_events:
# - "processing": Currently being processed
# - "processed": Successfully processed
# - "failed": Processing failed (check errorMessage)

###
